# Hama, the Bloodbender: "For as long as you control Hama" (CR 611.2b). Bot2 answers the enter trigger with Lightning Bolt on Hama, so Hama is
# gone when the trigger resolves: Bot2 still mills three (CR 608.2b: the trigger does as much as it can) and the Shock is still exiled, but
# Bot1 no longer controls Hama, so no one is given the right to cast it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Hama, the Bloodbender
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x6
Island
Island
Ornithopter
Shock
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: B)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hama, the Bloodbender.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Hama, the Bloodbender)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Hama, the Bloodbender; Black Lotus
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Shock)
? Exile = Shock
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Island; Lightning Bolt
! Bot1.Exile.Shock.Cast(Bot2)

[Expect]
Exile = Shock
